  "articleBody": "When you're thinking about adding safety rails to your bathroom, a common question is where exactly they should go – shower or tub? Well, it really depends on where you need the most support for your specific movements. For showers, you'll generally want horizontal bars on both side and back walls, typically placed around 33-36 inches high. This gives you something stable to hold onto when stepping in, out, and while standing. If you have a shower seat, a vertical bar nearby can also be super helpful for getting up and down. For tubs, a similar height range applies, but the placement needs to consider the tub's edge and how you transfer in and out. Think about where your hands naturally go for balance. It’s all about assessing your unique needs for standing, stepping, and transferring. Always remember, these rails need to be installed securely into wall studs or reinforced backing. If you’re not confident in finding those or dealing with tile, a pro can ensure everything is solid and safe.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}